      "notes": "makefile title=ruder, so the upstream ROM is ruder.nes; the bundled asset is renamed zap_ruder.nes to match its canonical id. The default make target is 'run'."
    },
    {
      "canonicalId": "builtin:concentration-room",
      "upstreamRepo": "https://github.com/pinobatch/croom-nes",
      "sourceRevision": "ed19c3c07ca389b70cf2e0dd2ce0320df28d511d",
      "sourceTarballSha256": "37c1f5dc90033b759a69fa1754b9dec9a1aa307eee8f2ed34dd15c5333a4d5c5",
      "buildEnv": "wsl-ubuntu-24.04",
      "buildWorkDir": ".",
      "buildSteps": [
        "make all"
      ],
      "outputRomPath": "croom.nes",
      "assetFilename": "concentration_room.nes",
      "mapper": 0,
      "romSha256": "3958bb569466b4f8894955b384f756681ecca1dc601d4ea373052371213f9061",
      "hashPolicy": "artifact",
      "notes": "makefile title=croom, so the upstream ROM is croom.nes; renamed to concentration_room.nes for the bundled asset. The default make target is 'run'. UNLIKE EVERY OTHER BUNDLED GAME, this upstream build is NOT byte-reproducible: tools/shuffle.py randomises the memory layout, and four clean builds with a fixed -r mode, a fixed --seed and PYTHONHASHSEED=0 still produced three different ROMs. hashPolicy=artifact therefore means: the shipped asset stays hash-pinned and verified, while a rebuild only has to prove that the pinned source still builds a valid ROM of the expected mapper and size."
    },
